# Read by Cloudflare from the ROOT of the uploaded assets, so the deploy moves this file up out
# of chromis/ - it is never served as /chromis/_redirects. Paths carry the /chromis prefix
# because the route hands the Worker the full request path.
#
# wrangler.jsonc turns html_handling off so that /chromis/privacy.html is served where it is
# instead of being redirected; these rules put back the three things GitHub Pages did for us.
# The first matching rule wins.

# The home page. A 200 here is a rewrite, not a redirect: the address bar keeps /chromis/.
/chromis/           /chromis/index.html    200
# The trailing slash matters, not just tidiness: every link in the site is relative, and from
# /chromis they would resolve against the domain root and miss.
/chromis            /chromis/              301
# GitHub Pages answered these with the page. Nothing here links to them, but anything outside
# that ever did should still land.
/chromis/privacy    /chromis/privacy.html  301
/chromis/terms      /chromis/terms.html    301
